  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Total number of stereoisomers in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>ox</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Br</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></mrow></msup></math> i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8771;</mo><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>AA</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>ab</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0200_c8ca9d94d30f.png\" style=\"width: 288px; height: 169px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> cis is optically active isomers and trans is optically inactive isomer</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Hence total isomers is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>"
